\section{Calculation Methods}{


Two modes are supported:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Unweighted} (default): Counts hourly RH values >= \code{rhlim} (0-24 hours)
\item \strong{Weighted}: Converts hourly RH to a wetness weight (0 at 80\%, 1 at
\code{rhlim}\%) and sums across 24 hours (0-24 wet-hours)
}

Rainfall contributes additional wet-hours (\code{RAIN / rainlim}, capped at 24)
combined with humidity wet-hours without double-counting by scaling to the
remaining dry fraction.

\strong{Fallback behavior:} If TMIN/TMAX are missing, returns binary wetness
(0 or 24 hours) based on \code{rhlim} and \code{rainlim} thresholds.
}

\section{Temperature and RH Interpolation}{


Hourly RH is derived from daily mean RH and temperature via:
\enumerate{
\item Compute vapour pressure from mean RH and mean temperature
\item Calculate hourly temperature using a sine/exponential diurnal model
\item Compute hourly saturated vapour pressure
\item Calculate hourly RH = 100 * (vapour pressure / saturated pressure)
}

This approach accounts for the fact that RH varies inversely with temperature
during the day (peaks at dawn/dusk, drops at noon) even when vapour pressure
is constant.
}

